{
  "about": [
    "Pregenerated parties for a playtest, so a developer with no characters to hand can still run their adventure.",
    "Each member has a `sheet` — an engine combatant spec, accepted as-is by encounter.create and adventure.encounter — and a persona the harness uses when briefing the seat. The two are kept apart because the engine refuses unknown spec keys, so `temperament` and `voice` may never be folded into `sheet`.",
    "The engine models no character building: there are no classes, species, backgrounds, feats, or levels here, and none of these numbers were derived from a class table. They are hand-picked to be ordinary for their tier, and the class-flavoured names are description only.",
    "Only four spells are executable in the bundled slice — Guiding Bolt, Shatter, Hold Person, Fireball — so the casters use those and nothing else. Positions are a loose marching order; the game master places the party for the scene.",
    "This is our own authored content, not transcribed from any source."
  ],
